mnemonics_and_roots:
  composite_memory_hook_en: Offering three acorns in the morning (朝三) and four at evening dusk (暮四) duped the monkeys and became a proverb for shifting capriciously (朝三暮四).
  composite_memory_hook_es: Ofrecer tres bellotas por la mañana (朝三) y cuatro al crepúsculo (暮四) engañó a los monos y dio origen al modismo de la veleidad (朝三暮四).
  cultural_and_cognitive_roots: Originating in the Daoist classic 《庄子·齐物论》, the keeper offered monkeys 3 acorns in the morning and 4 at night; when they raged, he offered 4 in the morning and 3 at night, pacifying them. Originally it illustrated the philosophical illusion of subjective gain and loss (两行), but over centuries shifted into condemning fickle inconstancy in human behavior.
  tone_sandhi_and_pitch_modulation: High, high, falling, falling: 'zhāo sān mù sì' (55-55-51-51). Articulate the first two syllables with level high pitch, followed by two crisp descending strikes.

